                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.841 Surtax/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-02T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                                1927—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>304. Your 781, August 1, 3 p.m. In discussions with your colleagues concerning
                    taxes and duties exacted by local Chinese authorities contrary to treaty
                    provisions you should be guided as regards this Government’s policy by
                    Department’s 302 of July 30, 7 p.m. and previous recent instructions. The
                    Department’s instructions do not preclude your discussing any form of joint
                    action your colleagues may propose, provided the use of military or naval force
                    is not involved. Inform colleagues at your discretion.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
